    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #347\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-140-auth-v1-02-08-implement-login-session-thr_x9sbe498q2` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #140: email/password login, session verification, logout, and independent remote session revocation for Semprec's `semprec-api` service, building on #139's auth schema and cryptographic primitives (rebased onto the latest `develop`, which had merged #139 after this worktree's branch point).\n\n**`backend/packages/data`** (business logic):\n- `errors.ts`: `UnauthorizedError` (401, generic message) reused for every login/session failure so no response reveals which condition applied.\n- `auth/sessionsStore.ts`: `revokeSessionForUser`, an ownership-scoped revoke.\n- `auth/authActions.ts` (new): `login` (Argon2id verify with timing-normalized dummy-hash comparison for unknown emails, one new session per call, records every attempt), `verifySessionToken` (hash → active-session lookup → `last_seen_at` bump), `logout` (revoke caller's own session), `revokeUserSession` (remote revoke of another of the same user's sessions, scoped by ownership).\n\n**`backend/services/semprec-api`** (HTTP surface):\n- `authHandler.ts` (new): `POST /api/auth/login`, `POST /api/auth/logout`, `POST /api/auth/sessions/:id/revoke`, `GET /api/auth/session`, plus the exported `authenticateRequest` middleware (accepts either the `semprec_session` cookie or `Authorization: Bearer`) that #143 can reuse for route-wide adoption.\n- Wired into `serve.ts`'s path dispatcher.\n\n**Tests**: new `authActions.test.ts` and `authHandler.test.ts` covering successful/failed login, cross-device session independence, cookie- and bearer-based verification, logout scoping, and cross-user revoke rejection.\n\n**Verification**: full build, lint, format check, dependency-boundary check, and the complete test suite (unit 97/97, integration 710/711, e2e 5/5) all pass. The one integration failure was a pre-existing, unrelated flaky concurrency test (`propertyTypeMigration.test.ts`) that passed cleanly on repeated runs and touches none of this issue's files.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
